# Cloudflare Pages rewrites.
#
# We need to:
#   1. Serve static SEO assets (robots.txt, sitemap.xml, og-default.png,
#      rss.xml, feed.xml, atom.xml) at their real paths, NOT through
#      the SPA fallback. Otherwise search crawlers and feed readers
#      see "index.html" for /sitemap.xml and /rss.xml — totally broken.
#   2. Keep the SPA fallback for everything else (Flutter web).
#
# Order matters: more-specific rules win, so the static assets are
# listed before the catch-all.

# Real SEO / feed assets — serve the files we shipped in /web/.
/robots.txt     /robots.txt    200
/sitemap.xml    /sitemap.xml   200
/og-default.png /og-default.png 200
/rss.xml        /rss.xml       200
/feed.xml       /feed.xml      200
/atom.xml       /atom.xml      200
# Google Search Console verification file. Body is
# `google-site-verification: googleBguSVNY65bi...html` (a single
# line, the standard Google file-format token). Belt-and-suspenders
# with the <meta> tag in index.html.
/googleBguSVNY65bi-pvRVGT8KqpBUnwMutY6BWAqkUBrKTR0.html /googleBguSVNY65bi-pvRVGT8KqpBUnwMutY6BWAqkUBrKTR0.html 200

# SPA fallback — every unknown path returns index.html so GoRouter
# can take over on the client. Required with PathUrlStrategy so
# /blog, /tools/merge, /pricing etc. all resolve correctly.
/*    /index.html   200
